@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Integrating with Azure Repos & GitHub";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Integrating Azure DevOps with **Azure Repos** and **GitHub** enables seamless source control, collaboration, and CI/CD automation. This integration streamlines software development workflows and enhances productivity.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Azure Repos?</h2>
        <p>Azure Repos is a **Git-based source control system** within Azure DevOps that helps teams manage and track code changes efficiently.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Provides **unlimited Git repositories** for teams.</li>
            <li>Supports **branching, merging, and pull requests**.</li>
            <li>Enables **permissions and policies** for secure development.</li>
            <li>Integrates directly with **Azure Pipelines** for CI/CD automation.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-repos.png" alt="Azure Repos" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Repos for Source Code Management</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Setting Up Azure Repos</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Navigate to **Azure DevOps > Repos**.</li>
                <li>Click **New Repository** and select Git.</li>
                <li>Clone the repository to your local machine.</li>
                <li>Commit and push changes to the repository.</li>
                <li>Create **branches and pull requests** for collaboration.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is GitHub?</h2>
        <p>GitHub is a **cloud-based platform** for hosting and managing Git repositories. It enables open-source and enterprise development collaboration.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Provides **public and private repositories**.</li>
            <li>Facilitates **code review through pull requests**.</li>
            <li>Offers **GitHub Actions** for CI/CD workflows.</li>
            <li>Integrates seamlessly with **Azure DevOps Pipelines**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Connecting GitHub to Azure DevOps</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Go to **Azure DevOps > Project Settings**.</li>
                <li>Under **Service connections**, select **GitHub**.</li>
                <li>Authenticate with your GitHub account.</li>
                <li>Select the repository you want to integrate.</li>
                <li>Use **GitHub Actions or Azure Pipelines** for CI/CD automation.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/github-integration.png" alt="GitHub Integration with Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Integrating GitHub with Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>CI/CD Integration with Azure Pipelines</h2>
        <p>Once your repositories are integrated, you can set up CI/CD pipelines to automate builds and deployments.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Define a **YAML pipeline** to trigger builds on code commits.</li>
            <li>Run **unit tests and security scans** as part of the build process.</li>
            <li>Use **multi-stage pipelines** for deploying to staging and production.</li>
            <li>Monitor pipeline execution using **Azure DevOps dashboards**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Source Control Integration</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Follow **branching strategies** like GitFlow for efficient collaboration.</li>
            <li>Use **branch policies** to enforce code reviews and quality checks.</li>
            <li>Enable **protected branches** to prevent accidental changes.</li>
            <li>Automate **pull request validation builds** to catch issues early.</li>
            <li>Regularly clean up **stale branches** to maintain a clean repository.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Integrating Azure Repos and GitHub with Azure DevOps enhances **collaboration, version control, and CI/CD automation**. By following best practices, teams can improve code quality and streamline deployments.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Running Automated Tests in Pipelines**.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("YAMLvsClassicPipelines", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: YAML vs Classic Pipelines</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("RunningAutomatedTestsPipelines", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Running Automated Tests in Pipelines &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
